{"requirements":[{"id":"create-local-ca","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority on node1 named OS Comparison Root CA.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A self-signed certificate with subject and issuer CN=OS Comparison Root CA was created with CA:TRUE and certificate-signing usage. Its public key matches the locally stored private key, which is root-owned and mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60e76f52501440e2","cmd-04965bda0b5b4959","cmd-cfd1f024c47149f9"]},{"id":"install-system-trust","requirement":"Install the new CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The certificate was installed in the RHEL trust-anchor directory, the system trust store was rebuilt, OpenSSL verification against the system bundle succeeded, and p11-kit reported it as an authority trust anchor. These results persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce3b852cbda34c55","cmd-04965bda0b5b4959","cmd-f920250192c4494b","cmd-cfd1f024c47149f9"]},{"id":"preserve-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after configuration and restart. OpenSSL was installed from the RHEL 10 repository and operated successfully on the node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e992bad578814502","cmd-a2bb605b563a4db8","cmd-f920250192c4494b","cmd-cfd1f024c47149f9","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing OpenSSL was a necessary prerequisite; creating the key and certificate and rebuilding trust directly implemented the task; and scheduling the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. The temporary certificate file was removed within the creation command. Afterward, package health was intact, no failed services or new listening services appeared, and temporary-file differences were normal reboot-generated systemd directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2bb605b563a4db8","cmd-60e76f52501440e2","cmd-ce3b852cbda34c55","cmd-4c6d802a60a14593","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot identity, returned to a running state, and retained the CA key, certificate, trust status, OS release, and kernel. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
